{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments ["<b>And he slaughters it, etc.</b> This refers to an ox or a sheep, but a lamb or a kid that grew in his domain and were changed through his hand — he is not liable, since he acquired them through a change, and what is his he sold or slaughtered. And this is likewise inferred from the words of the Sages (Bava Kamma 65a)." "<b>The ox.</b> In the Mishnah (Bava Kamma 62b) they said: one is liable for fourfold and fivefold payment only specifically for an ox or a sheep, and not for a wild beast or a bird. And their reasoning is that it could have said: ״כִּי יִגְנֹב אִישׁ שׁוֹר וּטְבָחוֹ אוֹ מְכָרוֹ חֲמִשָּׁה בָקָר יְשַׁלֵּם וְאַרְבַּע צֹאן תַּחַת הַשֶּׂה״, and one of them would be expounded to exclude everything outside of them, and through the addition of even one of them the intended meaning — that the law differs between the ox and the sheep — would have been audible."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:32:16.810545521Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}